" Tridactyl config. Sourced with:
"     :source --url http://127.0.0.1:8123/tridactylrc
" which needs no native messenger - `source --url` is a plain fetch, unlike
" `source <file>` which reads from disk and does.
"
" Served because ~/.config/startpage/tridactylrc is a symlink to this file and
" darkhttpd is already running for the startpage.

" --- new tab -----------------------------------------------------------------
" Why a local http page rather than an extension or file:// - see
" ~/.config/startpage/README.md. Short version: Tridactyl only injects into
" <all_urls>, which excludes moz-extension://.
" Literal 127.0.0.1, never `localhost`: /etc/hosts maps localhost to ::1 as
" well as 127.0.0.1 and the resolver returns ::1 first, while darkhttpd listens
" on 127.0.0.1 only. Every page load through the name therefore attempted IPv6,
" got refused, and fell back - measurable delay on every new tab.
set newtab http://127.0.0.1:8123

" --- theme -------------------------------------------------------------------
" Generated from ~/.config/theme/colors.sh by apply-theme.sh. --update forces a
" re-fetch; without it Tridactyl keeps the copy already in extension storage.
colourscheme --url http://127.0.0.1:8123/tridactyl-catppuccin.css --update catppuccin

" --- hinting -----------------------------------------------------------------
" Element highlighting is neutralised in the theme itself (both the direct and
" the overlay variables), leaving only a lavender ring on the active element.
" For pure Vimium style - hint labels and nothing else at all - instead set:
"     set hintstylesnohighlights true

" --- ignore ------------------------------------------------------------------
" Automatically enter ignore mode for below sites
blacklistadd ://youtube.com
blacklistadd ://figma.com
blacklistadd ://mail.google.com

" --- tab navigation ----------------------------------------------------------
" J = next tab (down the vertical tab list), K = previous (up) - the reverse of
" Tridactyl's defaults (J tabprev, K tabnext), which follow a horizontal strip
" read left-to-right. With vertical tabs (Zen; personal Firefox) "next" is
" DOWN, like vim's j. Set 2026-10-09. Tridactyl's config syncs through the
" Firefox account, so this applies to every browser signed into it.
bind J tabnext
bind K tabprev
